 don't think they're going to be  sitting there not being proud  it's terrible it needs to change but  ultimately  it doesn't stop us as black people  moving forward  near manchester a mural of marcus  rashford was defaced with racist  graffiti  it was then covered up in tributes to  him and is now being restored  in an emotional tweet he said i can take  critique of my performance  all day long but i will never apologize  for who i  am and where i came from that was mts  taeyab reporting from london it wasn't  all hate online marcus rashford also  posted some of the love  they've received from fans including  this letter from nine-year-old dexter  who wrote saying  i'm proud of you you will always be a  hero and from 11 year old alfie who said  i admire you and so should the rest of  the world  and another letter that said you should  be proud you made it to the finals you  tried your hardest  and that's very much good enough  messages of love and support there from  some soccers some of soccer's youngest  and perhaps wisest fans that 11 year old  alfie also wrote he said recently i've  been doing bad with my social anxiety  so my mom bought me your book and it  changed me  oh wow and this is one of the things  about marcus rashford he's done  an enormous amount of community support  he helped raise more than 27  million dollars to tackle food poverty  these are all these guys have been very  involved in the community  people should read a statement it's very  powerful he said i've been playing this  over  in my sleep he said i can do panel i can  do this in my sleep why it didn't work  that day  i'm so sorry he of course is beating  himself up yeah but you know how painful  this must be for all of them  yeah and i'm glad to see the outpouring  of support absolutely johnson prince  william speaking out  and this is this hurts in a way teaching  a lesson to these young kids and these  guys are leaders beyond the field you  know marcus absolutely yes topped the  uk's